# Python bytecode caches.
#
# Why this matters: previously the repo committed __pycache__/*.pyc files,
# so every `git checkout` shipped a stale .pyc snapshot from an old commit.
# When new keywords/imports landed in the .py source (e.g. learn_importance
# in egnn_dynamics.py, ELEMENT_IMPORTANCE in weighting.py), Python could
# still load the OLD .pyc and crash with errors like:
#   TypeError: EGNNDynamics.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'learn_importance'
#   ImportError: cannot import name 'ELEMENT_IMPORTANCE' from 'reactot.utils.weighting'
# Excluding them here + `git rm --cached -r **/__pycache__` makes the
# bytecode strictly machine-local, where it belongs.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Build / packaging
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Virtual envs
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Run artifacts (these can grow huge — keep them local)
checkpoint/
checkpoints/
logs/
results/
wandb/
ref_ts/
sb/

# Combo [FE]: x_0 predictor training data caches
data/x0_training_data/
